{
 "$doc": [
  "Scene table for tools/re/compare-frames.cjs (PLAN §8.3). Each scene sets the game up through LAST_EDEN with a",
  "small op list (coordinates in arcade px; {view:dx} = view.x+dx, {player:dx} = player.x+dx, 'M' = band mid,",
  "{lane:f} = band.top + f*(bottom-top); before G1 the ops are scaled to today's canvas px by AT.arc), renders,",
  "grabs the canvas and compares it with a reference frame: a frame of one of the two local videos (ffmpeg), a",
  "MAME snapshot (work/re/runs/<run>/snap-fNNNNNN.png or a crop of a verify composite) or an extract crop.",
  "`step` is the integration step after which the gates in `expect` are evaluated (earlier: the frames are still",
  "produced and the scene is reported 'early'). `expect` keys: heroHeight {h,tol}, bandTop (+soft), layout,",
  "recs [..], heldRec, role, pose, enemyState, overlay {minScore,mirror,search}, bossHeight {type,tol,ratio} (the boss",
  "rendered with and without its body, no step, gated on its ROM box), bossParts, paletteDiff {family,map,home,slots,minPens}, state, diffMax, roi.",
  "An `overlay` without minScore only records the fit score (used where the reference shows another hero).",
  "Every scene starts from a freshly loaded page (storage cleared) and Math.random is reseeded with `seed`, so a scene's frames are the same alone or in the table.",
  "Video timestamps were checked by eye on 2026-10-21 (work/re/visual/refs/*.png).",
  "G3a: `rig` {minScore, at, feet, tol, weaponTol, weaponScore, mirror} fits the hero exactly as HeroRig draws it (snapshot.player.anim + the held weapon, alone on a transparent canvas) into the reference over feet positions `feet` [x0,y0,x1,y1): score = share of its opaque pixels within `tol` (sum of channel deltas, 60) of the reference, `at` = the reference hero's feet (gate: within 1 px), the weapon refitted alone must sit within weaponTol px of where the body puts it. This is the PLAN §8.3 'overlay within 1 px of the MAME renders' gate.",
  "G3a: video references are compared by eye (PLAN §8.3 (b)); their `overlay` scores are recorded, not gated (s04-stand, s05-left/right show another stage, a walking frame, a hero cut by the screen edge or overlapped by the 2nd player). The MAME shots of the same stances carry the gates. The four MAME stances face right like the game hero, so their overlays no longer set `mirror`. s02-s05 tick 100 frames after start so the spawn invulnerability blink (alpha .65) is over before the silhouette is measured.",
  "G4: s08 spawns \"brute:B\" (test.spawnEnemy takes kind:variant since G4): the scene is BLK ELMER (Hutori B), while a plain brute is the kind's first variant, HAMMER T.",
  "G3c: s07 ticks 100 frames before damagePlayer(24) (the hit was ignored inside the 1.5 s spawn invulnerability, so the hero never fell). The ROM knockdown then plays: damagePlayer hits from behind, so Jack falls on knockFace (set3:7, 31 f with the KI11 trim: s07-fly at 6 f shows frame 0, s07-lying at 30 f the lying loop frame) and gets up on getup (set3:3, 25 f: s07-getup at 54 f). The MAME refs stay placeholders (see the scene note)."
 ],
